  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Thunderstorms today causing gusty outflows and heavy rain.\n\n- Steady precipitation tonight into Saturday south of I-90.\n\n- Warming and drying trend Sunday into the first part of next\n  week.\n\nSatellite and radar is showing the next round of showers and\nthunderstorms moving into Lemhi county and southwest Montana this\nmorning. The activity is expected to increase in coverage and\nintensity this afternoon. Storms this afternoon will be capable of\ngusty and erratic winds along with moderate to heavy rainfall.\nThis evening the storms will convert to stratiform steady rain\nwith the main focus of the precipitation being south of the I-90\ncorridor. \n\nA ridge of high pressure will be building over the region Sunday\ninto the first part of next week. This ridge will cause a warming\nand drying trend over the Northern Rockies.",
